                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Nelo is an amalgam of a bunch of cool and good ideas, but they are loosely connected with tape.\n\nThe game combines both melee action combat with third person and twin stick shooting elements.\n\nYou have different enemy classes, but their individuality gets lost when everything is shooting at you all at once. It takes away from strategizing which enemy should take priority over the rest and shifts to shooting everything on-screen to thin the herd. Playing on any difficulty than Recruit is a mistake.\n\nPlatforming was by far the worst thing experienced in the game. It was too floaty and just felt off.\n\nI also felt stages dragged on longer than should have, with them taking 30 minutes to an hour to complete. The mission objectives also left a lot to be desired. Obtaining orbs scattered across the stages to progress got old quickly.\n\nI can only recommend this to hardcore action game and shmup fans and with the caveat it's bought during a sale.\n\nPlayed version 0.1.4.1. I'm only giving it a positive rating because a lot of the ideas the game have were novel in 2017 and to an extent still is. And I would hope the developers return to the game in the future.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1788481166,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1788481166,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 0,
